<item name='HelpESubCat'><text>Access</text></item>
<item name='HelpFCategories'><text>2. Guide de gardien de base de données</text></item>
<item name='HelpFSubCat'><text>Accès</text></item>
<item name='HelpDocNumber'><number>2</number></item>
<item name='HelpSubCatNumber'><number>1</number></item>
<item name='HelpEHelpText'><richtext>
<pardef id='1' leftmargin='1in'/>
<par def='1'/>
<par def='1'><run><font style='italic'/>(NEW, this feature is part of the August 2009 release.)</run></par>
<par def='1'/>
<pardef id='2' leftmargin='1in' rightmargin='100%'/>
<par def='2'><run><font style='bold'/>Distinction between Soft Delete and Hard Delete</run></par>
<par def='2'>- Soft Delete: the documents are inactivated and made visible only in a special location for Administrators.  Only Orders can be Soft Deleted.</par>
<par def='2'>- Hard Delete: the documents Hard Deleted are no longer accessible.  When a Soft Deleted Order is deleted the result is a Hard Delete</par>
<par def='2'/>
<par def='2'><run><font style='bold'/>Who can delete documents? </run></par>
<par def='2'>1.To delete documents, the user must have the privilege "Delete Documents" in the Access Control List.  Note that the Administrators of the application should have this privilege</par>
<par def='2'>2. To delete documents, the user must have the role [Admin] in the Access Control List.  Note that the Administrators of the application should have this privilege</par>
<par def='2'/>
<par def='2'><run><font style='bold'/>Who can bypass the soft delete rules?</run></par>
<par def='2'>1. The users with the role [LNOG Admin] are asked if they want or not to use the deletion rules when deleting.  By selecting not to use the rules, they can hard delete directly any documents</par>
<par def='2'/>
<pardef id='3'/>
