<par def='2'/>
<par def='2'><run><font style='bold'/>Instructions to Soft Delete an Order</run></par>
<par def='2'>1. As an administrator, open the Order Tracking Application.</par>
<par def='2'>2. Click on one of the "View by".  (i.e. View by Date).</par>
<par def='2'>3. Select one or many order to soft delete. (The Soft Delete feature is applicable for any type of documents.)</par>
<par def='2'>4. Press "Delete" on your keyboard</par>
<par def='2'>5. The system will ask for your confirmation before doing the soft delete.  Answer "Yes"</par>
<par def='2'>6. The system will let you know that the Soft Deleted Orders can be found in the Administration menu under the link "Deleted Orders".</par>
<par def='2'>7. Go to the Administration menu and click on "Deleted Orders".  You will see all the Soft Deleted Orders.</par>
<par def='2'/>
<par def='2'><run><font style='bold'/>Instructions to Hard Delete an Order</run></par>
<par def='2'>1. As an administrator, open the Order Tracking Application.</par>
<par def='2'>2. Go to the Administration menu and click on "Deleted Orders".  You will see all the Soft Deleted Orders.</par>
<par def='2'>3. Select one or many order to hard delete.</par>
<par def='2'>4. Press "Delete" on your keyboard</par>
<par def='2'>5. The system will ask for your confirmation before doing the hard delete.  Answer "Yes"</par>
<par def='2'>6. The system will mark the documents for deletion by adding a check mark in front of them.</par>
<par def='2'>7. To finish the deletion you have to press F9 to refresh the view and you will be asked to delete the documents or not.  Answer Yes.</par>
<par def='1'/>
<par def='1'><run><font style='bold'/>Rules about the deletion:</run></par>
<par def='1'>1. <run><font size='11pt'/>Users without the role [Admin] cannot flag documents for deletion</run></par>
<par def='3'><picture height='117px' width='628px'><notesbitmap>
